r_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T00:08:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T00:27:33Z","body":"> Currently only focuses the text area with the hotkey, just clicking the script tab does not focus it (I was having trouble finding the spot for this in the code, would appreciate some insight from others).\r\n\r\nNot certain if this is the best solution, but here how I currently imagine it:\r\n\r\nFor shortcuts and wherever it gets focused, there can be a callback in EditorDock called from `_make_dock_visible` where it focuses the tab bar and maybe for floating windows too.\r\n\r\nFor clicking on the tab, I think `DockTabContainer` or `EditorDockManager` needs to connect to the dock containers `tab_clicked` signal. ~Or maybe even the `tab_selected` signal? Not sure if that would steal focus when its unwanted.~ And it should not be just for `EditorMainScreen`, since it should probably apply to ShaderEditor too (and if they can ever move to other slots). This should also call the callback.\r\nAnd ScriptEditor has the callback to essentially call `ScriptEditor::focus_editor`.\r\n\r\nEdit: `tab_selected` would cause issues I think especially with shader editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5689907297/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5699632910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122910#issuecomment-5699632910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122910","id":5699632910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU7l_Dg","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T15:00:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T15:00:53Z","body":"I reached out on Rocket Chat (or we can continue on Github if you prefer). I was misunderstanding this line (but I get it now)\r\n> For clicking on the tab, I think DockTabContainer or EditorDockManager needs to connect to the dock containers tab_clicked signal.\r\n\r\nThough to make things less convoluted, what do 